1
00:00:04,630 --> 00:00:06,530
(Sheldon:)You know, it just
occurred to me,

2
00:00:06,540 --> 00:00:09,790
(Sheldon:)if there are an infinite
number of parallel universes,

3
00:00:09,790 --> 00:00:12,800
(Sheldon:)in one of them,
there's probably a Sheldon

4
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:16,220
(Sheldon:)who doesn't believe
parallel universes exist.

5
00:00:16,220 --> 00:00:18,600
(Leonard:)Probably. What's your point?

6
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:19,520
(Sheldon:)No point.

7
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:20,850
(Sheldon:)It's just one
of the things

8
00:00:20,850 --> 00:00:22,640
(Sheldon:)that makes one of
the mes chuckle.

9
00:00:23,970 --> 00:00:27,060
(Sheldon:)What makes you
chuckle, Leonard?

10
00:00:27,060 --> 00:00:29,560
(Leonard:)Hmm, recently?

11
00:00:29,560 --> 00:00:30,680
(Leonard:)Not much.

12
00:00:30,680 --> 00:00:32,700
(Sheldon:)Is it because of the
conflict that arises

13
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:35,020
(Sheldon:)from your desperate need
to pair-bond with a woman,

14
00:00:35,020 --> 00:00:37,240
(Sheldon:)and the apparent collective
decision of all womankind

15
00:00:37,240 --> 00:00:41,660
(Sheldon:)to deny you
that opportunity?

16
00:00:41,660 --> 00:00:43,130
(Sheldon:)Um...

17
00:00:43,130 --> 00:00:45,630
(Leonard:)Shut up.

18
00:00:45,630 --> 00:00:48,030
(Leonard:)You know,
when my grandfather died,

19
00:00:48,030 --> 00:00:50,500
(Sheldon:)and Meemaw was alone,
my mom arranged for her

20
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:52,500
to visit a center
three times a week

21
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:56,060
(Sheldon:)where she could socialize
with other lonely people.

22
00:00:56,060 --> 00:00:57,420
(Sheldon:)It's very nice.

23
00:00:57,420 --> 00:01:01,210
(Sheldon:)They discuss current events,
play bridge, get a hot meal.

